  "conclusion": "Procedural exact-seat binary calibration materially improved held-out value MAE, RMSE, and correlation, and PUCT-8 repeated a small +2-win uplift on each of two disjoint windows. A high-retention student nevertheless matched the source exactly on a fresh 128-game zero-search gate. A zero-sum multiplayer target improved regression metrics but lost two held-out PUCT wins and was rejected. Pairwise ranking produced the best value metrics and a combined +21.25 baseline-adjusted Elo over 256 PUCT games, but its second window was negative, so it remains unconfirmed and was not distilled. No artifact was promoted. More data or a larger teacher is required before another procedural PUCT distillation attempt."
